-----
      Pre-built binaries for VAX/VMS and VMS-specific packaging of the
 NetHack sources are both available over the network, but not directly
 from linc.cis.upenn.edu due to disk space considerations.

      The (4) packages are available from two different hosts, and both
 of those hosts are reachable via anonymous ftp from the Internet and
 via DECnet from NSI/DECnet (formerly SPAN).

              host name       (numeric address)          directory
 tcp/ip   uars.acd.ucar.edu     128.117.32.2         [.SRC.NETHACK]
          hamlet.caltech.edu    131.215.139.3        [.NETHACK]
 DECnet   ACDURS::               9.367  (9583::)     SYS$LCL:[SRC.NETHACK]
          HAMLET::              14.850  (15186::)    ANON_ROOT:[NETHACK]

      There is a "readme" file plus four large files, each containing a
 BACKUP saveset packaged inside a VMS text library.  The text library file
 contains binary data with fixed-length 512-byte records and has built-in
 compression enabled.  Here are the 4 files, with their sizes listed.

                                                               size-in-blocks
                                                              library  saveset
   NETHACK-EXE.TLB       -- executable and data for VMS         2123    3024
   NETHACK-OBJ.TLB       -- compiled object modules for VMS     4217    5544
   NETHACK-SRC-VMS.TLB   -- sources used for VMS port + data    4605    8631
   NETHACK-SRC-OTHER.TLB -- additional sources (other ports)    3330    5418
                                                       total   14275   22617

      NETHACK.README describes the contents plus unpacking procedures.
 No 3rd-party software is needed to unpack, but quite a bit of disk space
 is required (during unpacking, the peak amount needed is the sum of the
 library size plus twice the saveset size).  Generally only one of the
 first three files is needed; building from the sources is recommended.

      The pre-compiled object files and the pre-built executable and
 "playground" directory are for VAX/VMS.  NETHACK.EXE was linked under
 VMS V5.1-1 and should run under V5.1 and up; tested under V5.5-2.  The
 object files could be relinked under older versions.  The sources can
 be unpacked and built as-is under Alpha/VMS (aka OpenVMS AXP).
